# Semgrep's built-in ignore list silently drops tests/ from every scan. On this
# repo that meant a CI job whose stated scope was the whole repository (`.`)
# actually read 30 of 55 tracked Python files: all 25 files in tests/ were
# skipped, reported only as "Files matching .semgrepignore patterns: 25".
#
# This project's tests are gates, not scratch code, so they are in scope. A
# .semgrepignore in the repository root replaces the built-in list rather than
# adding to it, which is the point: everything excluded is excluded here, on
# purpose, and tests/ is not among it.

# Vendored or generated; not this project's source.
node_modules/
.venv/
.git/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
build/
dist/
site/
coverage.xml

